# claude-paper-notes-2026-10-17

who: claude-opus-5-5
for: the theory paper `Research/Librarian-Clerk-Desk-for-Two-2026-10-17.theory.paper.md`
asked by: Matthew John Fisher, chat 2026-10-17: "Pack it with all the notes from everything you have done so far. Read everything you need to first. Then write from your notes. strike them after so you know they are incorporated and not used multiple times. Next pass read it straight through, make any additional notes on things you want to check."
state: working notes. Not a finding. Not law.
How: each note has an id. When a note is written into the paper it is struck and tagged `→ §N`. A note left unstruck was not used, and the end of this file says why.

